'What worked: CBEngine supplied nearly all early product names, descriptions and vendor IDs. Its2008 taxonomy was Home & Family → Kids/Parenting; later menus used Parenting & Families → Parenting/Education/Pregnancy/Special Needs. Category samples span2008,2009,2010,2012,2013 and2016. Archived official ClickBank feeds supplied additional2017 and2022 observations. Vendor activation dates and tracker “First Seen” dates were not substituted for capture years.','',
'Seller domains were resolved primarily from the "'`CBRehoppp2` target embedded in saved CDX original URLs under `<vendor>.hop.clickbank.net`, and secondarily from explicit affiliate-resource URLs in feed descriptions. This inspects the archived redirect destination without requesting the seller page. Targets were URL-decoded, never inferred from product titles. Tracking parameters are retained. Redirect destinations are historical metadata and need Phase2 confirmation. If two rows share an evidenced domain, the later row is marked `DUPLICATE DOMAIN`.'"','',
'What did not work: the ClickBank2008 index was a static category navigator with no product names; its exact marketplace.htm URL had no2014–2020 records. CBTrends’ old numerical category IDs were reused for finance categories; those were not treated as parenting evidence. The fetched2010 Kids URL rendered “Home” and unrelated products. CB-Analytics’ encoded category captures returned broad/default listings or empty categories, and the exactSIGNBABY product lookup returned no records. JVZoo2014/2019 launch lists and the WarriorForum2010 affiliate database were populated but contained no useful niche offers. Broad product-index and some hop CDX queries returned503s/timeouts; failed queries are distinguished from successful empty listings below. No fetched page was classified as a JavaScript-only product app.','',
'The official feeds have **no structured seller-URL field**. Only a few descriptions supply URLs. Their original ZIP payloads are preserved as "'`.txt.zip`; exact XML members were extracted locally as `clickbank-feed-2017-v1.xml`, `clickbank-feed-2022-v1.xml` and `clickbank-feed-2022-v2.xml`. Use those XML files for title/description evidence: the initial normalized feed `.txt` conversion stripped CDATA. The original capture text and ZIPs were left unchanged. The two2022 feed formats largely duplicate the same products and were not counted twice.'"','',
