# Phase 1A — ClickBank marketplace history

Run date: 2026-11-03. Read `sales-letters/README.md` first. Output: [candidates-A.tsv](../candidates-A.tsv). Evidence review: [p1a-evidence-review.md](p1a-evidence-review.md).

28 offer rows; 7 rows have an evidenced seller domain (7 unique domains); 21 retain unresolved domains. 11 rows are explicitly sleep-adjacent. Several remaining rows have age, format or therapeutic-scope cautions. This is a candidate queue, not a list of verified qualifying sales letters. No seller sales page was fetched.

Request accounting: **99 counted requests**: 98 instrumented request attempts (retries included), 0 instrumented followed redirects, and one initial CDX call before instrumentation. The initial successful HTTP call did not log automatic redirects; reserving the urllib limit of ten additional redirects gives a conservative **maximum of 109 Wayback requests**, within the 120-request cap. The instrumented hard stop was 109 requests, including any logged redirects. Detailed evidence: [`p1a-requests.jsonl`](../../_raw/sales-letters/_discovery/p1a-requests.jsonl), [`p1a-commands.jsonl`](../../_raw/sales-letters/_discovery/p1a-commands.jsonl), [`p1a-helper-stderr.log`](../../_raw/sales-letters/_discovery/p1a-helper-stderr.log).

All Wayback traffic used `python3 -I _tools/wayback.py`, sequentially, with its shared four-second throttle. No live site visits. CDX windows were primarily 2008–2020, extended to 2005–2022 for feed and hop metadata. Actual product observations span 2008–2022; capture years in the TSV are discrete observations, never a claimed continuous sales period.

What worked: CBEngine supplied nearly all early product names, descriptions and vendor IDs. Its2008 taxonomy was Home & Family → Kids/Parenting; later menus used Parenting & Families → Parenting/Education/Pregnancy/Special Needs. Category samples span 2008,2009,2010,2012,2013 and 2016. Archived official ClickBank feeds supplied additional 2017 and 2022 observations. Vendor activation dates and tracker “First Seen” dates were not substituted for capture years.

Seller domains were resolved primarily from the `CBRehoppp2` target embedded in saved CDX original URLs under `<vendor>.hop.clickbank.net`, and secondarily from explicit affiliate-resource URLs in feed descriptions. This inspects the archived redirect destination without requesting the seller page. Targets were URL-decoded, never inferred from product titles. Tracking parameters are retained. Redirect destinations are historical metadata and need Phase 2 confirmation. If two rows share an evidenced domain, the later row is marked `DUPLICATE DOMAIN`.

What did not work: the ClickBank 2008 index was a static category navigator with no product names; its exact marketplace.htm URL had no 2014–2020 records. CBTrends’ old numerical category IDs were reused for finance categories; those were not treated as parenting evidence. The fetched2010 Kids URL rendered “Home” and unrelated products. CB-Analytics’ encoded category captures returned broad/default listings or empty categories, and the exact SIGNBABY product lookup returned no records. JVZoo 2014/2019 launch lists and the WarriorForum 2010 affiliate database were populated but contained no useful niche offers. Broad product-index and some hop CDX queries returned503s/timeouts; failed queries are distinguished from successful empty listings below. No fetched page was classified as a JavaScript-only product app.

The official feeds have **no structured seller-URL field**. Only a few descriptions supply URLs. Their original ZIP payloads are preserved as `.txt.zip`; exact XML members were extracted locally as `clickbank-feed-2017-v1.xml`, `clickbank-feed-2022-v1.xml` and `clickbank-feed-2022-v2.xml`. Use those XML files for title/description evidence: the initial normalized feed `.txt` conversion stripped CDATA. The original capture text and ZIPs were left unchanged. The two 2022 feed formats largely duplicate the same products and were not counted twice.

The helper gained optional request logging/cap, HTTPS selection, link/raw/header sidecars, CDX collapse/filter/status options, ZIP/XML handling and `fetch --no-redirect`. Defaults remain compatible. The final hop-index sweep used one attempt per lookup to protect the remaining budget. Empty prices mean no consumer price was evidenced; research-tool membership fees, commission percentages and affiliate earnings were excluded.

Excluded or kept outside the candidate queue: Kidzgrow tracking software (format mismatch); GeniusMaker software/age uncertainty; Eye Can Too! Read (Pre-K–grade 8); generic school reading/spelling materials; prenatal intelligence offers; non-English products; fertility, gender selection, breastfeeding, baby names, baby showers and generic parenting. Early Educators Resources targets classrooms rather than mothers; CoordiKids lacks baby-age/format evidence. Toddler Speech Delay is retained only as explicitly therapeutic adjacent, outside Mamivio claim lines.

Ten priorities for Phase 2, ranked as hypotheses about long-form selling potential. None is yet confirmed to meet the ≥1,200-word/price-or-buy-CTA definition:

